1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,960
This man threw away a hard drive.

2
00:00:02,590 --> 00:00:04,272
At its peak, it was worth

3
00:00:04,272 --> 00:00:05,530
about a billion dollars.

4
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:08,200
In 2009, James Howells,

5
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:10,170
a computer engineer in Wales,

6
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:11,621
mined eight thousand

7
00:00:11,621 --> 00:00:12,910
bitcoins on his laptop.

8
00:00:12,910 --> 00:00:15,180
They were worth almost nothing.

9
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,601
He kept the keys on an old

10
00:00:16,601 --> 00:00:18,060
hard drive, in a drawer.

11
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:20,582
In 2013, while he was clearing

12
00:00:20,582 --> 00:00:21,190
out the house,

13
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:23,550
it went into a bin bag by mistake,

14
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:25,270
and the bag went to the dump.

15
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:27,360
Months later, Bitcoin exploded,

16
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,550
and he realized what he'd thrown away.

17
00:00:29,950 --> 00:00:31,560
He begged the council to let him dig.

18
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:33,010
They said no.

19
00:00:33,010 --> 00:00:33,632
He offered them

20
00:00:33,632 --> 00:00:34,610
a quarter of the fortune.

21
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:38,250
He brought investors, AI scanners,

22
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:39,600
even robot dogs. Still no.

23
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:41,270
And the price kept climbing.

24
00:00:41,670 --> 00:00:43,365
He sued the council for almost

25
00:00:43,365 --> 00:00:44,860
five hundred million pounds.

26
00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:46,520
The judge threw it out.

27
00:00:46,870 --> 00:00:48,660
He even offered to buy part of the dump.

28
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:51,320
The council plans to close it for good.

29
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:53,480
After twelve years, he gave up.

30
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:55,880
The hard drive is still down there.

31
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,240
Would you have kept digging?
